From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: xxxvik-xakerxxx <19531907+xxxvik-xakerxxx@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 11:20:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] drm/panel: accept S6E8FC3X02 panel revisions

The initial compile-only port admitted only display ID 40 21 01, but that
value has no counterpart in the Nothing OS 4.1 driver.  A clean native boot
on a Tetris A015 reads the valid three-byte ID 40 41 02 and is rejected
after all initialization commands have completed.

The official driver uses the DT compatible to select S6E8FC3X02 and exposes
the three ID bytes as revision information without an allowlist.  Follow
that model: retain the full-length transfer check and log the detected ID,
but do not reject an otherwise valid panel revision.

Signed-off-by: xxxvik-xakerxxx <19531907+xxxvik-xakerxxx@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-samsung-s6e8fc3x02.c | 9 ++-------
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-samsung-s6e8fc3x02.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-samsung-s6e8fc3x02.c
index 3ba6df1..657a1e8 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-samsung-s6e8fc3x02.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-samsung-s6e8fc3x02.c
@@ -276,8 +276,7 @@ static void s6e8fc3x02_panel_init(struct s6e8fc3x02 *ctx,
 
 static int s6e8fc3x02_check_id(struct s6e8fc3x02 *ctx)
 {
-	static const u8 expected_id[] = { 0x40, 0x21, 0x01 };
-	u8 id[ARRAY_SIZE(expected_id)];
+	u8 id[3];
 	int ret;
 
 	ret = mipi_dsi_set_maximum_return_packet_size(ctx->dsi, sizeof(id));
@@ -297,10 +296,6 @@ static int s6e8fc3x02_check_id(struct s6e8fc3x02 *ctx)
 		return dev_err_probe(&ctx->dsi->dev, -EIO,
 				     "short panel ID read: %d\n", ret);
-	if (memcmp(id, expected_id, sizeof(id)))
-		return dev_err_probe(&ctx->dsi->dev, -ENODEV,
-				     "unexpected panel ID %*ph\n", (int)sizeof(id), id);
-
-	dev_info(&ctx->dsi->dev, "panel ID %*ph verified\n",
+	dev_info(&ctx->dsi->dev, "panel ID %*ph detected\n",
 		 (int)sizeof(id), id);
 	return 0;
 }
